      "text": "<|channel|>analysis<|message|>The user asks: \"Write a simple website in HTML. When a user clicks the button, it shows a random joke from a list of 4 jokes.\" So we need to provide an HTML file with JavaScript to handle button click and random selection from an array of jokes. Keep it simple. Provide code snippet. Include CSS maybe minimal. Provide explanation. Ensure that it works. Use <html>, <head>, <body>, <button id=\"jokeBtn\">Get Joke</button>, <p id=\"jokeDisplay\"></p> and script.\n\nLet's produce final answer.<|end|><|start|>assistant<|channel|>final<|message|>Here’s a single, self‑contained HTML file you can save as `index.html`.  \nWhen you open it in a browser and click the **“Tell me a joke”** button, a random joke from the array is shown underneath.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <title>Random Joke Generator</title>\n  <style>\n    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 2rem; }\n    #joke { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }\n    button { padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem; font-size: 1rem; cursor: pointer; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n  <h1>Random Joke Generator</h1>\n  <button id=\"jokeBtn\">Tell me a joke</button>\n  <p id=\"joke\"></p>\n\n  <script>\n    // 1. List of jokes\n    const jokes = [\n      \"Why don’t scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!\",\n      \"I told my wife she was drawing her eyebrows too high. She looked surprised.\",\n      \"Parallel lines have so much in common. It’s a shame they’ll never meet.\",\n      \"I can’t believe I’d ever feel disgusted at the word ‘sandwich’.”\"\n    ];\n\n    // 2. Reference to the button and the paragraph that will display the joke\n    const btn = document.getElementById('jokeBtn');\n    const display = document.getElementById('joke');\n\n    // 3. Click handler\n    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {\n      // Pick a random joke\n      const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);\n      const joke = jokes[randomIndex];\n\n      // Display it\n      display.textContent = joke;\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. The `<script>` block holds an array called `jokes` with four strings.\n2. We grab the button (`#jokeBtn`) and the paragraph (`#joke`) with JavaScript.\n3. When the button is clicked, a random index is chosen, and the corresponding joke is set as the paragraph’s text.\n\nFeel free to add more jokes, change the styling, or embed this snippet into a larger project. Enjoy the laughter! 🚀",
